# EMDR — accessibility panel

`AccessibilityWidget` is the floating Nura mark button that opens a settings panel
(text size, contrast, targets, spacing, links, motion). It sits on the marketing
shell and under `/app`. Read this before touching it or the CSS it depends on.

## Files

| Job | Path |
|---|---|
| Types, validation, attributes, bootstrap script, edge dock | `lib/a11y-preferences.ts` |
| Ribbon + panel, drag, storage | `app/components/AccessibilityWidget.tsx` |
| Widget styling (ribbon, edges, panel) | `app/components/accessibility-widget.css` |
| The effects on the page | `app/globals.css` → last block, **Accessibility preferences** |
| Pre-paint apply | inline script in `app/layout.tsx` (`a11yBootstrapScript()`) |
| Tests | `tests/a11y-preferences.test.ts` |

## How it works

1. Preferences are stored in `localStorage` (`nura.a11y.v1`), **not** on the account.
   Guests on the marketing site get them too.
2. They are applied as attributes on `<html>`: `data-a11y-text`, `data-a11y-contrast`,
   `data-a11y-targets`, `data-a11y-spacing`, `data-a11y-links`, `data-a11y-motion`.
   A preference that is off **removes** its attribute, so the shipped CSS stays in charge.
3. `a11yBootstrapScript()` re-applies them in `<head>` before first paint, so the page
   never flashes at the wrong text size. Keep `A11Y_ATTRIBUTES` as the single source of
   truth: the script is generated from it and a test asserts the script sets every key.
4. Text size scales the **root font size** (100 / 106.25 / 112.5 / 118.75%), which scales
   every rem in the app. Each step also sets `--a11y-scale` for fixed-pixel chrome that
   must grow with its text (currently the `/app` sidebar rail).

## Rules

- **Never** scale `html` font size without adding the matching `--a11y-scale` and a test
  case. `tests/a11y-preferences.test.ts` reads `globals.css` and fails when a step or an
  attribute loses its styling block.
- The effects block must stay **last** in `globals.css`: it is an override layer, so
  source order decides against the base tokens.
- The widget is an **edge-docked ribbon**, not a free-floating button. Folded it is a
  30×88 half-pill flush to the edge with a chevron; open it is the 52px Nura mark plus a
  small fold control that pushes it back into the edge. It is **folded by default**.
- **One click on the folded ribbon unfolds it and opens the settings** — do not add a
  second step. Accessibility controls must stay one tap away.
- The folded ribbon is **draggable**: drag along the edge to move it, drag past the
  middle to re-dock on the other edge. Arrow keys do the same (up/down move, left/right
  re-dock). Persist through `saveDock`; clamp the vertical center with
  `clampA11yCenterY`, never by hand, and never write to storage on every pointermove
  (write on the pointerup that ends the gesture).
- The default edge is a **prop** (`<AccessibilityWidget defaultEdge="left" />`): marketing
  docks left (help pill and back-to-top own the right), `/app` docks right. Do not move
  that decision into CSS — `data-edge` is always set by JS.
- Bottom bars (`.fe-cookie-banner`, or add `data-a11y-lift` to a new one) reserve room so
  a dragged widget cannot sit under them: the widget measures the tallest visible one and
  passes it as the `bottomInset` of `clampA11yCenterY`. A new full-width bottom bar must
  be added to `BOTTOM_BANNER_SELECTOR` or the widget can overlap it.
- **Place the panel from the target box, not a measured rect.** The ribbon morphs
  (width/height/top transition), so `getBoundingClientRect()` mid-transition reports the
  collapsed ribbon and the panel lands on top of the button. Take the stable used value
  of `left`/`right`, add `A11Y_FAB_SIZE`, and read the saved center from the inline
  `--a11y-center`.
- The button is hidden while a set runs (`body:has(.app-shell.session-immersive)`), same
  as the Help FAB. The settings themselves always stay applied.
- Accessibility controls are not decoration: do not hide the widget behind consent,
  a login, or a modal.

## Adding a setting

1. Add the field to `A11yPreferences` + `DEFAULT_A11Y_PREFERENCES` in `lib/a11y-preferences.ts`.
2. Add it to `A11Y_ATTRIBUTES`, `a11yAttributeValues`, and `a11yBootstrapScript`.
3. Add a toggle row in `AccessibilityWidget` (`TOGGLE_ROWS`) or a new control.
4. Add the CSS block in `globals.css` under the matching `html[data-a11y-…]` selector.
5. Cover it in `tests/a11y-preferences.test.ts` (parse, attributes, CSS contract) and
   check it at ~390×844.

## Copy

English, sentence case, no em dash. Short labels plus one plain hint line per row
(what it does, not how it works). Follow `redpen` for anything longer.

## Do not

- Do not add dark mode, colour pickers, or font-family swaps here: the Nura palette and
  Source Sans 3 are fixed (`nura-brand`).
- Do not `!important` the reduced-motion reset per component. It is global on purpose:
  `animation-duration`/`transition-duration` collapse to `0.001ms` with one iteration.
- Do not rely on `prefers-reduced-motion` alone for JS motion. Landing GSAP checks
  `isA11yReduceMotionPreferred()`; do the same in new JS animation.
